# Emergency braking (docs/emergency_stop.md) on the burn-in axis (10 mm a
# revolution): at 188 rad/s (300 mm/s) something fails; hv0.sim_dist,
# zeroed then, is how far the axis went (1 rad = 1.59 mm). Coasting takes
# ~16 rad (26 mm) and ~180 ms.
# An HV board fault (here HV_VOLT_ERROR reported by the F3, hv0.sim_fault =
# 11): the power stage can't be trusted, so no stop: outputs off, the axis
# coasts, whatever the stop modes say.
@args --drive ../hwtest/burnin/ECMA-C30604FS/stmbl.conf
@timeout 120
lcnc 0 0
run 0.5
lcnc 1 0
run 1.5
lcnc 1 300
run 1
hv0.sim_vel
hv0.sim_dist = 0
hv0.sim_fault = 11
run 0.004
fault0.stop
run 0.3
hv0.sim_dist
fault0.fault
@expect fault0.stop[1] == 0
@expect hv0.sim_dist > 14
@expect fault0.fault == 11
